<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:19Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Israel: Netanyahu supporters gather as PM votes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:54a985ea65dc771bef044288f801eedd660ada563e5f61dc6ca8dceded1c75f3</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:09Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T14:37:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-netanyahu-supporters-gather-as-pm-votes--3f57cd1da13b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-netanyahu-supporters-gather-as-pm-votes" /><summary type="html">Supporters of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu gathered outside a polling station where the leader was voting on Tuesday. This is Israel's first election since the October7, 2023 Hamas attack and is seen as a referendum on Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali reports from Jerusalem.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: A referendum on 'Bibi' Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb8cc31eb61c6f0d8830bffd0468b611cffd1dd3eb7f0d05727b001792cd0f6e</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:00Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:52:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261027-israeli-election-a-referendum-on-bibi-netanyahu--42870793125e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20261027-israeli-election-a-referendum-on-bibi-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Tuesday, October 27: The Israeli, Palestinian and Lebanese papers break down what's at stake on election day for Israel and its neighbours. Also, the French government announces its first major concessions to protesting high school students, hoping to calm the movement. Finally, Harry Kane's Ballon d'Or means Lamine Yamal and Kylian Mbappé will have to wait their turn.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli PM casts his ballot as voters voice opposition to Netanyahu outside polling stations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1329bb8d1c9f3dd9f88077cb3441aa01da9a7629180220a0d58ea51240ec6d50</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:03Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T12:42:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-pm-casts-his-ballot-as-voters-voice-opposition-to-netanyahu-outside-polling-stations--664441f7283c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-pm-casts-his-ballot-as-voters-voice-opposition-to-netanyahu-outside-polling-stations" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu cast his vote on Tuesday (October 27) in Israel’s general election. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iraqi court sentences six French nationals to life for IS group membership</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b53011054b461cd82064092117ded062bfcd4d03d9db9347bfcaa4f4b7c8d416</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:39Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:16:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-iraqi-court-sentences-six-french-nationals-to-life-for-is-group-membership--3e5d4146faaa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-iraqi-court-sentences-six-french-nationals-to-life-for-is-group-membership" /><summary type="html">Six French men were sentenced to life in prison by an Iraqi court on Tuesday for membership of the Islamic State (IS) group, according to a source. They are ​among ‌47 French IS group suspects transferred from ⁠detention facilities in Syria to Iraq last year under an arrangement coordinated by US forces and Iraqi authorities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli election: Fragile co-existence between residents in Jewish-Arab town of Lod</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3353aa258d49757ec7259437c64df7a1d4602d52016a39c3f7b7ff0dac074e70</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:14:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261027-israeli-election-fragile-co-existence-between-residents-in-jewish-arab-town-of-lod--de028a4ce766.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261027-israeli-election-fragile-co-existence-between-residents-in-jewish-arab-town-of-lod" /><summary type="html">As Israelis head to the polls this Tuesday, among those voting are 2 million Palestinian citizens of Israel, some of whom live in mixed Jewish-Arab towns. One of them, Lod, has long been seen as symbolic of this coexistence. However in 2021 the town was the scene of violent clashes, whose consequences are still being felt. FRANCE 24's Stéphane Amar, Sandra Lederer and Josh Vardey report.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Syria slams deadly Jordan strikes as ‘unacceptable’ breach of airspace</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b2e3636e9d14ea665eeaebd55ce8053f830071a2fdb60829772ad688951b29d</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:48Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T11:02:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-syria-slams-deadly-jordan-strikes-as-unacceptable-breach-of-airspace--2b9a8e2f5e25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-syria-slams-deadly-jordan-strikes-as-unacceptable-breach-of-airspace" /><summary type="html">Syria's foreign ministry on Tuesday condemned Jordanian strikes in southern Syria in retaliation for a deadly church attack in the kingdom last week that Amman linked to militants operating across the border. Syria said the strikes killed seven ⁠people, including three children and a woman. Jordan said it regretted the civilian casualties.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Jordan launches airstrikes in Syria after church attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:110e18a89835e42b85bdff4ab07ad727ad2ebf1468d4e817a76cc7f82deb588f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:59:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/jordan-launches-airstrikes-in-syria-after-church-attack--27982e6f3f71.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/jordan-launches-airstrikes-in-syria-after-church-attack" /><summary type="html">Jordan carried out airstrikes Monday (October 27) evening against armed groups in Syria in retaliation for Friday’s attack on a Greek Orthodox Church in the southern Jordanian city of Karak that killed nine people, the Jordanian air force said in a statement. Syrian authorities said at least six people were killed.</summary></entry><entry><title>Palestinians in West Bank fear further escalation of violence if Netanyahu remains PM</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c93b210df9b52e587fac2602c0d2d2f4c19d1723d864843e234e7112515bd6ef</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:50:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/palestinians-in-west-bank-fear-further-escalation-of-violence-if-netanyahu-remains-pm--1f5e2d22638e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/palestinians-in-west-bank-fear-further-escalation-of-violence-if-netanyahu-remains-pm" /><summary type="html">Ramallah residents say they hope to see Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu lose power in elections. "Netanyahu remaining in power means that there will be a clash, a build-up of tension and an explosion in the region", says one resident. Israel has committed the crime against humanity of "extermination" in the West Bank, while continuing to commit "genocide" against Palestinians in the Gaza Strip, United Nations-mandated investigators said Monday (October 27).</summary></entry><entry><title>Israelis vote in first national election since October 7 attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4972b6d921db56ebc47417fa1a39982ed5937f97bd414330fb73b197b42cf52d</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:42:58Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:41:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israelis-vote-in-first-national-election-since-october-7-attack--c484a521ac8a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israelis-vote-in-first-national-election-since-october-7-attack" /><summary type="html">Israelis are voting in a pivotal election Tuesday (October 27) as their country wrestles with unresolved wars, continues to reel from Hamas' 2023 attack and is deeply divided over the character of the state and the right person to lead it. FRANCE 24's Clovis Casali tells us more from the ground. He spoke with voters.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu's political survival on the line as Israel heads to the polls</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:af57efa9af97e68f0b1369269635b5a5fd611c43cf7d9738b8aa793f68369467</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:07Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:14:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-s-political-survival-on-the-line-as-israel-heads-to-the-polls--b5fbf6bedec9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-s-political-survival-on-the-line-as-israel-heads-to-the-polls" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu faces a fight for political survival in Israel's election on Tuesday (October 27), with voters weighing his leadership after the 2023 Hamas-led attacks, wars in Gaza and with Iran, and Israel's deepening international isolation. FRANCE24's Douglas Herbert gives us his analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli elections: voters turnout reaches '16.7%' four hours after polls open</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abb892ea751fd91e10d8e8e301a77bff29d5a7f00d9479ea08a07695e39fc961</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:13Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T10:08:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israeli-elections-voters-turnout-reaches-16-7-four-hours-after-polls-open--17a1ea46300d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-elections-voters-turnout-reaches-16-7-four-hours-after-polls-open" /><summary type="html">A deeply divided Israel headed to the polls on Tuesday (October 27) for the first time since the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack, with voters delivering their verdict on veteran Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and the country's rightward drift. FRANCE 24's Noga Tornapolski tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Netanyahu blasts Arab parties for ‘trying to steal’ vote as Israel holds tense election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0d882c00baf8e33f8aa52f3ec1848ebdd0e8d13232ccb4113a5ad3956b04e6ea</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:16Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T08:15:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack--7c2b87d7e0f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-live-polls-open-in-first-israeli-election-since-october-7-attack" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Tuesday renewed his attacks on Arab parties, warning after casting his ballot that "they're trying to steal the election" after reports that individuals were arrested with envelopes of cash. The deeply divided country is voting in its first national elections since the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack. Follow our live blog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Polls open in Israeli election seen as referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:754df0caee1898225f2d2b7348d7ecf66aa9b27c1a7ab3b342a917a41526b46e</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:43:19Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T07:14:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-israeli-election-seen-as-referendum-on-netanyahu--52acafb6ca86.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/polls-open-in-israeli-election-seen-as-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Polls opened Tuesday in Israel’s critical national election viewed as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu’s policies. Reporting from Jerusalem, FRANCE 24’s Noga Tarnopolsky explains that “the name of the game” after Election Day is whether the country’s fractious opposition, including an Arab-Israeli majority bloc, can come together to form a government.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israelis vote in tense election seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b93221df97186b58ea70176e371b2c6adc8465b232b3e02748c30d8c7fd43be</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-27T04:12:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-2026-netanyahu-october-7--393517cfbc4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261027-israel-election-2026-netanyahu-october-7" /><summary type="html">Israelis are voting Tuesday in the first general elections since the October 7, 2023, Hamas attack with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu facing a fight for political survival. The vote follows three years of regional wars, with Netanyahu running neck and neck with centrist rival Gadi Eisenkot.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Mecca pact nations hold talks with Iran to prevent renewed Middle East war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33530430b49574d1ae3e0fe77401471b9778609bab34dc300fc896f929174a2b</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T23:24:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-iran-talks-mecca-pact-nations-war--271d84436965.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-iran-talks-mecca-pact-nations-war" /><summary type="html">Senior officials from Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan held talks in Iran on Monday aimed at preventing renewed fighting in the Middle East, with Tehran describing discussions as “very good”. The diplomatic push, attended by Saudi Defence Minister Prince Khalid bin Salman, followed warnings from Washington, Tehran and Israel of renewed hostilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UN cites 'ethnic cleansing' concerns around Israel's Palestinian displacement operation in Hebron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f63c1f841e7cdb99a9b115bc3baa68cbf88504acebb9f0611b905030c42c4b4</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:59:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron--f54dc7b36717.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-un-cites-ethnic-cleansing-concerns-around-israel-palestinian-displacement-operation-hebron" /><summary type="html">The United Nations on Monday raised "ethnic cleansing" concerns following Israel's operation to displace by force more than 3,000 Palestinians from their homes in Hebron in the West Bank after two Palestinian gunmen killed two Israeli soldiers at a checkpoint near the city on Friday. UN rights chief Volker Turk said in a statement that the "aggressive operation" must end, and that "collective punishment is a grave violation of international law".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Opponents accuse Netanyahu of stoking tensions with Iran before Israel's election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:724fce2e8a856e1d5d73fbb0c056ffb087b3d3aff487d5e1b5daafaba6e27fe6</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T17:11:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election--5429441497ca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/opponents-accuse-netanyahu-of-stoking-tensions-with-iran-before-israel-s-election" /><summary type="html">Israel's defence minister denied on Monday (October 26) reports of a rift between PM Netanyahu and the army over Iran, before the vote.  Netanyahu has campaigned heavily on his security credentials, insisting only he can "finish the job" in the US-Israeli war on Iran. His main rival, ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot, has accused him of playing up the Iran threat when it suits him politically, and of failing to accomplish his war goals. FRANCE 24's Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli candidate Eisenkot pledges to unite country as Netanyahu deems him 'soft' on Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cda5e778a2d36402e000c353bc68fb2b26da746121316bd5541fa56dde68e4a4</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:58:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran--bd8634a89185.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-israeli-candidate-eisenkot-pledges-to-unite-israelis-as-netanyahu-deems-him-soft-on-iran" /><summary type="html">Israeli presidential candidate Gadi Eisenkot's pledge made Sunday to "heal" Israeli society after Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's divisive tenure resonated with some voters attending his final campaign rally before polling begins Tuesday. Netanyahu meanwhile received fresh backing for re-election from US President Donald Trump and deemed Eisenkot "soft" on Iran.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel election: unable to vote from abroad, expats have to fly home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f2cccb1dc4b2f0ef06f6c85c54e56dad509e1f0b24812e8e7d16901742f6bc3</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T16:47:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home--cdb70f36234d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-election-unable-to-vote-from-abroad-expats-have-to-fly-home" /><summary type="html">Israelis can’t vote from abroad, so tens of thousands of expats are expected to fly home for the election. At Tel Aviv airport, supporters of opposition figure Gadi Eisenkot are already waiting at arrivals. A “Fly and Vote” initiative helps expats organise their trip, despite a failed petition from Netanyahu’s Likud party to restrict it. With polls predicting a tight race, every vote could count, and the result will decide the Prime Minister’s fate.</summary></entry><entry><title>Jordan's strikes on Syria over church terror attack kill several civilians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf8921329ae8f17679b36fe9bae6a467b06e98afa4bd9743f4f5c8582c31fdd0</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T15:12:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-jordan-arrests-three-following-deadly-terror-attack-on-church--ff7fe6210ee5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261026-jordan-arrests-three-following-deadly-terror-attack-on-church" /><summary type="html">Jordanian authorities on Monday arrested three suspects over last week's terror attack that killed nine people in a church funeral procession in the village of Hammoud. Jordan's military later launched strikes on "terrorist organisations" in neighbouring Syria in retaliation for the attack by alleged Islamic extremists, killing at least eight civilians including women and children, a health official said.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands of Israelis living abroad expected to fly in for pivotal vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0e00b463b9434b494dbdda080ae2a452a561df6b0755119fa79e0e40e359dd1</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T14:20:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote--a3d6b8696ede.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tens-of-thousands-of-israelis-living-abroad-expected-to-fly-in-for-pivotal-vote" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27). Unable to vote from abroad, tens of thousands of expatriate citizens have been flying in from across the world to cast their ballots. FRANCE 24's Noga Tarnopolsky met some of them at the airport.</summary></entry><entry><title>Will Netanyahu's security promise win him this election?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e4db50e9915c5c1d14d2342b10d0288a03330d02b254aa0e72b29b350c48acc</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T13:52:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election--7245e677289a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-will-netanyahu-s-security-promise-win-him-this-election" /><summary type="html">Since the beginning of his political career, Benjamin Netanyahu, Israel's longest-serving prime minister, has campaigned on a promise that he is the only one who will keep the Jewish state safe. As Israelis head to the polls for their first election since the October7 Hamas attacks and the start of the war in Gaza, Netanyahu's strategy might be less effective. FRANCE 24's Gabrielle Nadler explains.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel braces for national elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcb12a8f45892b4d2a02d6a956ef0516843c9c640f540516cb95dc160aa9c439</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:35:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-braces-for-national-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu--603ad1ac5180.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-braces-for-national-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis are preparing to head to the polls on Tuesday (October 27)  in the first elections since the October 7th attacks in 2023. Unable to vote abroad, expatriate citizens have been flying in from around the world to participate in a vote widely seen as being a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Arab Israeli voters could prove decisive in the upcoming elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7db3333c3465dfd0bba35cb8ee6e3679be3ab7c31989b8a6095d41bbd0cb167c</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T12:13:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-arab-israeli-voters-could-prove-decisive-in-the-upcoming-elections--cf7c16524fa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-arab-israeli-voters-could-prove-decisive-in-the-upcoming-elections" /><summary type="html">In Israel’s election the vote of Arab Israeli citizens could be crucial for the outcome and fate of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu who is standing for re-election. Traditionally voting turnout is lower among Arab Israelis than among the rest of the population. But this time some feel it’s their duty more than ever to cast their ballot given the policies and wars undertaken by Netanyahu.</summary></entry><entry><title>A look at the main issues in Israeli elections seen as a referendum on Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e191088ed8e9eb937ba979d54ab60798bbeab1381bfe3fec10edaa990f17432</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:59:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-a-look-at-the-main-issues-in-israeli-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu--91568101be2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261026-a-look-at-the-main-issues-in-israeli-elections-seen-as-a-referendum-on-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israelis will vote Tuesday (October 27) in the first national elections since Hamas' Oct. 7, 2023, attack in what is widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's leadership. He rejected ICC war crimes claims and denied corruption as national elections approach. Details by FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem, Noga Tarnopolsky.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israeli election seen as a referendum: For or against Netanyahu?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0af5732e28e4f847004712c0e15aa567860996e9523d0ac60326fe55f58ca5f</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-26T11:40:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261026-israeli-election-seen-as-a-referendum-for-or-against-netanyahu--842384761d07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261026-israeli-election-seen-as-a-referendum-for-or-against-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has led his country almost continuously for nearly 17 years. But will he manage to retain power following Tuesday's election? Netanyahu's latest term has divided Israeli society more than ever and will be marked by the October 7 attacks, his handling of the conflicts in Gaza, Iran and Lebanon, as well as his controversial judicial reform. FRANCE 24's David Gilberg reports, with Lauren Bain.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Report: IDF chief pushes back on Netanyahu's order</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d2beb377825be5d62a8171b2abc420b0bb2cbb38282448d2c7ea0ca9d448f89</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T23:24:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261025-report-idf-pushes-back-on-netanyahu-s-order--18329c3cde80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261025-report-idf-pushes-back-on-netanyahu-s-order" /><summary type="html">An extraordinary confrontation at the top of Israel's leadership, just two days before the election. Israeli media report Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and military chief Eyal Zamir are at odds over Iran. Zamir reportedly fears government instructions could trigger an immediate military escalation and has demanded written authorisation. Netanyahu denies any confrontation. The reports come as he warns Iran could attack Israel to disrupt Tuesday's vote.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel: Demonstrators rally against government ahead of election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f6521a29606b417b22c5935c3bacfc25e824391d0210c89af005c47b0dce59da</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:38:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election--605d00c22edc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-demonstrators-rally-against-government-ahead-of-election" /><summary type="html">In Israel, the anti-Netanyahu movement is mobilising. Thousands gathered in Tel Aviv on Friday to protest against the Israeli government, just three days ahead of a general election widely seen as a referendum on Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu.</summary></entry><entry><title>West Bank: Families forcibly displaced in Hebron</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57612e45304ac41a7d4a7a4ad7622fa4ad4ce6b57d92608f7cf7a2e04071b273</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-25T11:35:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron--c0b8d6b2a6c9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/west-bank-families-forcibly-displaced-in-hebron" /><summary type="html">More Palestinian families have been displaced in the occupied West Bank as Israeli forces continue operations in Hebron, following a deadly shooting that killed two Israeli soldiers on Friday. With elections scheduled for Tuesday, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has vowed a heavy response to the attack. Morgaene Ayre has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands take to Tel Aviv's streets for protests against Netanyahu</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2959af4cb0f67595cde5674f4417c8c9dd4ea8f3f7c6861fabf7112c2714b89</id><updated>2026-10-27T14:41:06Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T18:21:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu--99da939090a4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261024-thousands-take-to-tel-aviv-streets-for-protests-against-netanyahu" /><summary type="html">Thousands marched against Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's government in Tel Aviv on Saturday – just three days before Israel's general election – demanding accountability for the failure to prevent a Hamas-led attack on October 7, 2023, which led to the war in Gaza.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
